matrix_data.Yoda:
Yoda is a research data management service that enables Utrecht University researchers and their partners to collaborate, deposit, publish and preserve research data.
-Data is stored in a safe where it can not be changed or deleted. Encrypted replicas are archived outside the institution by EUDAT, the European research data infrastructure;
-Data are grouped into data sets defined by user group that can be enriched with metadata;
-Persistent identifiers (DOIs) are created to make your published data sets citable;
-Versions of the datasets can be kept in order to monitor the use of data during all stages of the research;
-User management tools can be used to authorize both internal and external users to use your datasets;
-Your data is accessible as a network folder (Windows, Mac OS, Linux) wherever you are.
